# Plaza walkable surface + HZD walls for s99a.
#
# Floor: one 200x200 OBJ-unit quad at Y=0 covers the whole walkable
# area (= 20,000 PSX units after scale x100). The bunker interior
# shares the same Y=0 floor — no separate strip needed. Emitted as a
# single HZD_FLR quad; hzd_writer no longer fan-splits OBJ quads into
# two degenerate-triangle floors.
#
# Walls: OBJ `l` primitives become HZD_SEG vertical wall segments.
# Each `l v1 v2` is one wall. PSX HZD walls are infinite-vertical,
# so the y component just goes along for visualization. The perimeter
# wall has a 30-OBJ-unit gate gap on the south side (X=-15..+15);
# the bunker forms a closed box (the door is rendered visually but
# the HZD treats the bunker's south wall as continuous-solid so the
# closed door blocks the player).

# Floor + perimeter corner verts.
v -100 0 -100   # 1: NW
v  100 0 -100   # 2: NE
v  100 0  100   # 3: SE
v -100 0  100   # 4: SW

# Gate corner verts on the south perimeter.
v  -15 0  100   # 5: gate left
v   15 0  100   # 6: gate right

# Bunker corner verts (X=-60..-20, Z=-60..-20).
v -60 0 -60     # 7: bunker NW
v -20 0 -60     # 8: bunker NE
v -20 0 -20     # 9: bunker SE
v -60 0 -20     # 10: bunker SW

# Plaza floor (single quad → one HZD_FLR quad).
f 1 2 3 4

# Perimeter walls (north, east, south split, west).
l 1 2
l 2 3
l 4 5
l 6 3
l 4 1

# Bunker walls — closed box.
l 7 8
l 8 9
l 9 10
l 10 7
